00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.460
First question is coming from Avinash.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.380
And Avinash says, hey, Evan, I'm really stuck

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:31.940
in my career and life, not knowing where to head next.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.280
And worse, not knowing how to find out.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.060
I need guidance to break free and come out of it.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.360
Could you help me?

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.300
Okay.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.980
So, I'm excited to hear what you have to say

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.460
about this, Evan, actually.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.220
Because I was thinking about some practical skills

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.400
to get unstuck.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.460
And I think that a lot of us feel stuck.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.460
And it's a, I think it's definitely complex.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.160
But I think one of the first things I would say,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.680
just on a practical level, is, you know,

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.480
when you're stuck, you feel frustrated

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.100
because you want to see more momentum.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:22.120
And so that can, in a lot of us,

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:27.120
that can create this kind of urgency to go and do.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.800
And, you know, there's nothing wrong with that.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.120
And I think that could be, at different times,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.680
the right strategy.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.880
But I was just, the first thing that came to mind

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.800
is when you're feeling stuck,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.480
one of the best things I think you can do

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:47.040
is just kind of like get still,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.820
turn out all the noise,

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:52.820
and I don't know if you like to journal,

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.880
I don't know if you like to just sit

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.160
and ponder and contemplate.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:00.480
I don't know if you like to pray or meditate.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.300
But like, there's just different things you can do

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.940
to kind of connect more deeply.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.120
And I think sometimes you get stuck

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.080
when you're kind of running without a vision,

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.220
running without clear purpose,

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.520
you're not connected to who you are.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.920
And so, I don't know,

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.360
I just think it might seem counterproductive

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.800
to not just go out and do something,

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.780
but I think it is important that before you do

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.120
that next thing, to get still

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:35.760
and kind of get refocused on who you are,

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.960
what you want to do, and kind of your why.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.920
Like, why am I going to do this,

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.040
whatever this next thing that I'm going to do is.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.160
So, those are some hopefully practical steps.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.320
For me, I think it starts with,

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.680
do you have something that you want to do?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.760
Do you have, you know, I've always wanted to X,

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.380
I've always wanted to go salsa dancing,

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.680
I've always wanted to launch a website,

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.320
or I've always wanted to build an app,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.700
or I've always wanted to play guitar,

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.860
or whatever it is, even if it doesn't make sense.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.460
You know, I would never have thought

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:17.460
that I would invest in and later acquire

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:21.260
North America's largest salsa dancing school

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.420
when I first walked into a salsa dancing college, right?

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.260
Yeah.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.960
I would never have expected that.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.900
But I wanted to learn how to dance.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.900
You know, it was just something interesting to do.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.500
And at the same time as I did that,

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.060
I did, you know, 20 other things

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.460
that I didn't continue with.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:39.660
And that's okay.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.660
So it's finding within yourself,

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.940
is there something that you want to do,

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.180
and then finding some small way to get started

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.680
without putting so much expectations on it.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.840
I think people set this, that set themselves up for failure

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.820
because they put too high expectations on themselves.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.000
Like, I'm going to go in and that first class

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.680
has to be amazing, and this has to be

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.300
my next business opportunity,

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.380
and this has to be the thing that I'm going to do

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.940
for the rest of my life, or I'm not going to do it.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:10.260
So there's so much pressure on that first day

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.300
that then you quit and move on to something else.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.380
Well, that could have been an amazing thing.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.960
And so, for the people who know what they want to do,

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.260
for sure, then go out and chase that.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.500
You know, and you may have a whole bunch

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.120
of limiting beliefs around why you can't,

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.380
but it doesn't sound like it's the case here.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.500
It doesn't know what the next thing is to do.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.900
So I'd start by thinking about

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.260
what are some of the things that I've always wanted to do

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.380
that I have an interest in.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:38.300
You know, I did this when I sold my business.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.700
When I sold my first company,

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:43.540
I didn't, there was this big hole in my heart.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.620
You know, like, what do I do next?

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:46.940
It was a great problem to have.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:47.940
I'm not complaining about it,

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.780
but it was still a problem in that

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.940
I didn't have a clear plan of what I wanted to do next.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.780
It was, I don't want to say depressed,

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.740
but you know, as someone who likes having plans

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.000
and likes knowing what they're doing,

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.240
that was a not great place to be in for me.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.160
And one of the things I wanted to learn about

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.640
was venture capital.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.360
You know, I never needed to raise venture capital

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.200
for my company, but I wanted to learn about it,

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.320
and I ended up connecting with a venture capital company

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.640
and learning the ropes,

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.380
and I was there for a couple years,

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:25.700
and it was interesting, and I enjoyed it.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:30.580
At the same time, I started doing, you know,

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:33.560
more salsa dancing, getting more active in it.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.340
I started doing public speaking,

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.460
and I did a whole bunch of other stuff

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.900
that I don't remember that didn't stick.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:44.100
And so it's just exploring the things

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.080
you've always wanted to do in a small way

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.460
and seeing how much you like it

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:51.060
without putting the pressure on it having to work out.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.420
Just like if you go on a first date with someone,

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.980
it doesn't have to be that person you're going to marry yet.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.060
You know, you're going to set yourself up for failure

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.020
if you have to decide after the first date

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.620
if you're going to marry somebody.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.280
If you have no idea, you don't know what you want,

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.960
like there's zero inclination,

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:14.260
there's nothing you've always wanted to do,

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:17.660
even to try, you feel totally lost,

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.380
then I would say just start exposing yourself

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:21.380
to more opportunities.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.060
Just say yes, the whole bunch of stuff.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.100
Adopt a mindset of that you'll try anything once.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.660
It's a good mindset to have in general.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:33.940
Try anything once, whether it's a new activity,

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.900
whether it's going to a new place,

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.740
whether it's trying a new food,

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.340
you're unhappy and feel stuck

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.340
because you're doing the same thing

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.380
over and over and over and over again.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.260
So saying yes to things,

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:51.280
even if you judge them initially as being not for you

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.980
and having no interest in it,

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.820
just saying yes and trying things

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.020
until you find something that you do

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.980
want to go back and do it again.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:03.260
I really love that spicy Indian food.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.100
Let me go back and try some more of it

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.480
or maybe I'll go cook some of it on my own

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.680
and that leads you down this path.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.020
And you'll find that you hate a lot of the stuff

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.620
or it's not interesting for you.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:20.660
You don't like snowboarding or whatever it is that you try.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.620
So be open, say yes.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.820
Adopt a mindset of trying anything once

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.180
until you find the thing that you want to do

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:33.020
again and again and again and again because you love it.

